# React Component Boundaries

**Trigger**: Auto-applied to all `.tsx` and `.ts` files in `app/` and `components/`.

## Server vs Client Component Classification

Every component file must be classified as exactly one of: **Server Component** or **Client Component**. Mixed files are forbidden.

### Client Component Detection

A file is a **Client Component** if ANY of the following appear anywhere in the file:

- `"use client"` directive at top
- `useState`, `useEffect`, `useReducer`, `useRef`, `useCallback`, `useMemo` hooks
- `usePathname`, `useRouter`, `useSearchParams` from `next/navigation`
- `useTheme` from `next-themes`
- DOM access: `window`, `navigator`, `document`, `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`
- Event handlers on JSX: `onClick`, `onChange`, `onSubmit`, `onKeyDown`, etc.
- Custom hooks that use any of the above

### Server Component Rules

**Server Components are the default.** Only add `"use client"` when a Client-Only trigger is present.

Server Components MUST NOT:
- Import hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`, etc.) directly or indirectly
- Use browser-only APIs
- Contain event handlers on JSX elements
- Import from packages that are client-only (e.g., `next-themes`)

### Component Composition Pattern

When a Server Component needs interactivity, split into two files:

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — Server Component fetches data, passes to Client Component
// app/dashboard/page.tsx
export default async function Page() {
  const data = await fetchData();
  return <InteractiveWidget data={data} />;
}

// components/dashboard/interactive-widget.tsx
"use client";
import { useState } from "react";

export function InteractiveWidget({ data }: { data: Post[] }) {
  const [filter, setFilter] = useState("all");
  // ... interactive logic
}
```

### The "use client" Placement Rule

**Always at the very first line of the file**, before imports:

```tsx
// ✅ CORRECT
"use client";

import { useState } from "react";
import { Card } from "@/components/ui/card";
```

### Phosphor Icons Import by Component Type

This is the most common source of hydration errors:

```tsx
// Server Component (has no "use client")
import { IconName } from "@phosphor-icons/react/ssr";

// Client Component (has "use client")
import { IconName } from "@phosphor-icons/react";

// Shadcn UI components (always "use client")
import { IconName } from "@phosphor-icons/react";
```

### Nesting Rules

| Parent | Can Contain | Cannot Contain |
|--------|------------|----------------|
| Server Component | Server Components, Client Components | Direct hooks, browser APIs |
| Client Component | Client Components only | Server Components as children |

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — Server wraps Client
// app/page.tsx (Server)
import { DashboardContent } from "@/components/dashboard/dashboard-content"; // has "use client"
export default function Page() {
  return <DashboardContent data={data} />;
}

// ✅ GOOD — Client wraps Server-imported components as children
// This works because the Server component's output is just JSX props,
// not a nested Server Component boundary
```

### Dynamic Icon Pattern (Server-Safe)

When mapping icon names to components in a Server Component:

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — all icons imported from /ssr, mapped via switch
import { House, PencilSimple } from "@phosphor-icons/react/ssr";
import type { Icon } from "@phosphor-icons/react";

function getIcon(name: string): Icon {
  switch (name) {
    case "house": return House;
    case "pencil-simple": return PencilSimple;
    // ...
  }
}

const IconComponent = getIcon(item.icon);
<IconComponent className="size-4" />
```

### Third-Party Context Providers in Server Components

Any library component that uses React hooks internally (`useContext`, `useState`, etc.) crashes with "Cannot read properties of null (reading 'useContext')" when rendered in a Server Component. The React dispatcher is null during server rendering.

**Audit rule**: Before importing any third-party component, check if it uses hooks. If unsure, assume it does and wrap in a Client Component.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — SessionProvider uses useContext internally, crashes in Server Component
// app/layout.tsx (Server Component)
import { SessionProvider } from 'next-auth/react';

export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return <SessionProvider session={session}>{children}</SessionProvider>;
}

// ✅ GOOD — import a Client Component wrapper
// app/layout.tsx (Server Component)
import { Providers } from '@/components/providers'; // has "use client"

export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return <Providers session={session}>{children}</Providers>;
}
```

**Common context providers that crash in Server Components**: `SessionProvider` (next-auth), Radix UI primitives (TooltipProvider, Dialog, etc.), theme providers, any `createContext` consumer.

### Common Mistakes to Avoid

| Mistake | Problem | Fix |
|---------|---------|-----|
| `"use client"` missing from file using `useState` | Runtime error | Add `"use client"` at top |
| CSR phosphor import in Server Component | Hydration error, context mismatch | Use `/ssr` subpath |
| `next-themes` import in Server Component | Browser-only API crashes on server | Move to Client Component |
| `usePathname` in Server Component | Hook not available in RSC | Move to Client Component |
| Module-level JSX with React state (e.g. status icon objects) | Evaluated at module scope in Server Component | Move JSX inside function body or use `"use client"` |
| Client Component wrapping server-only data fetch | Defeats purpose of Server Components | Fetch in Server, pass as props |
| Third-party context provider in Server Component | `"Cannot read properties of null (reading 'useContext')"` | Wrap in Client Component |
| Importing from `radix-ui` instead of `@radix-ui/react-*` | Types-only package has no real React components | Use actual `@radix-ui/react-*` packages |

### Dashboard Layout Special Case

Dashboard layouts (`app/(dashboard)/layout.tsx`) are Server Components that render client-side components (`SidebarNav`, `MobileMenu`, etc.) as children. This is the correct pattern:

```tsx
// layout.tsx — Server Component (no "use client")
import { SidebarNav } from "@/components/dashboard/sidebar-nav"; // has "use client"
import { MobileMenu } from "@/components/dashboard/mobile-menu"; // has "use client"

export default function DashboardLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <div>
      <SidebarNav items={navItems} />
      <main>{children}</main>
    </div>
  );
}
```

The layout itself does NOT need `"use client"` because it only passes props to Client Components.

## Verification

Before committing:

- [ ] Files with hooks have `"use client"` at the top
- [ ] Server Components don't import client-only packages
- [ ] Phosphor imports match the component type (`/ssr` for Server, main for Client)
- [ ] No `usePathname`/`useRouter` in Server Components
- [ ] No `useTheme` in Server Components
- [ ] `pnpm run build` passes (no hydration errors)
